#!/usr/bin/env python3
#
# Equivalence test: test_prom_mdk_memory's counted verdict against real
# captured MDK memory-battery transcripts, without booting anything
#
# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
"""
A plain unittest -- no QEMU, no qemu_test import, runnable with just
`uv run --with pytest pytest
tests/functional/mips64/test_prom_mdk_memory_verdict.py -v`. The memory
battery's tests end with identical completion words, so its verdict
counts rather than matches; these fixtures prove the counting against
real transcripts.

Fixture provenance (real captured guest-console text, byte-exact; none
synthesized):

  REAL_MEMORY_PASS_TRANSCRIPT
      The mdk.log of the first real meson run of test_prom_mdk_memory
      itself (func-mips64-prom_mdk_memory OK in 1033s, 2026-08-27,
      run.json beside it in that build tree): the path-structured
      netboot and all eight tests passing.

  REAL_FLAT_NAME_TRANSCRIPT
      The transcript of the project checkout's
      docs/boot-logs/firmware.mdk-memory-suite.2026-08-26T23:42-07:00:
      the first-ever run of the battery here, served FLAT
      (`bootp()/memory.mdk`), with two extra interactive probes the
      functional driver never sends -- an `ls`, and the vendor manual's
      `mem.dr` name, answered with the kernel's own not-found line.
      Triple duty: the real "flat name" FAIL fixture for the path
      assertion; proof the count equalities hold on a real all-pass run
      (its eight completions are the same eight tests); and proof that
      interactive noise and a probed not-found do not read as failure --
      which is exactly why "Command not found" is not a failure marker
      here (a driven test that does not exist already fails the counts).

  REAL_NEVER_REACHED_PREFIX
      A real prefix of REAL_MEMORY_PASS_TRANSCRIPT, cut before the
      BASEIO PROM loads. Verbatim, truncated, not edited.
"""

